{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   The user (via the cobbler orchestrator) has assigned task #5402: implement srd058-rm requirements R1.1-R1.4 for `cmd/rm`. This is a \"stitch\" task in a code generation pipeline. The task requires:\n   - R1.1: When given FILE arguments, remove each file using unlink(2)\n   - R1.2: Without -r flag, refuse to remove directories and print error to stderr\n   - R1.3: Never remove '.' or '..', print error if specified\n   - R1.4: When removal fails (permission denied, etc.), print error to stderr and continue with remaining files\n   \n   The task explicitly scopes OUT R2 (recursive/force), R3 (interactive/verbose), and R4 (exit codes/diff testing beyond basic R1 needs), but stubs for those must still compile. Test cases covering R1.1-R1.4 must be added to the differential test file.\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - Differential testing pattern: Run Go binary and GNU reference binary (grm) side-by-side, compare stdout/stderr/exit code\n   - `pkg/testutils.RunDiffTests` and `DiffTest` struct for test cases\n   - `pkg/testutils.BuildBinary(t, \".\")` to compile the cmd package under test\n   - `exec.LookPath(\"grm\")` with `t.Skip` if reference not found\n   - `sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()` at start of main\n   - `os.Remove()` for file removal (Go's equivalent of unlink)\n   - `os.Lstat()` to check file type without following symlinks\n   - Exit code 0 on success, 1 on any failure\n   - GNU rm error message format: `rm: cannot remove 'PATH': REASON`\n   - 40-line function limit (E8), 500-line file limit (E9)\n   - No git commands allowed - orchestrator handles git\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - `docs/specs/software-requirements/srd058-rm.yaml`\n     - Full SRD with R1-R4 requirement groups, non_goals, and acceptance criteria\n     - R1 (Basic file removal) is the scope of this task\n     - Non-goals: no --one-file-system, no --preserve-root/--no-preserve-root, no shred-on-delete\n\n   - `cmd/rm/main.go` (existing contract stub to modify)\n     - Already has complete flag parsing in `parseFlags()` \n     - Has `options` struct with recursive, force, dir, interactive, verbose fields\n     - Has `interactiveMode` enum (interactiveNever, interactiveOnce, interactiveAlways)\n     - Has `isDotOrDotDot()` helper already implemented\n     - Stub functions to fill in: `removeFiles`, `removeFile`, `removeDir`, `removeEmptyDir`, `promptRemoval`, `shouldPromptOnce`\n     - Current `removeFiles` just prints \"not implemented\" and returns 1\n     ```go\n     func removeFiles(paths []string, opts options) int {\n         fmt.Fprintf(os.Stderr, \"rm: not implemented\\n\")\n         return 1\n     }\n     func removeFile(path string, opts options) error {\n         return fmt.Errorf(\"not implemented\")\n     }\n     func removeDir(path string, opts options) error {\n         return fmt.Errorf(\"not implemented\")\n     }\n     func removeEmptyDir(path string, opts options) error {\n         return fmt.Errorf(\"not implemented\")\n     }\n     func isDotOrDotDot(path string) bool {\n         return path == \".\" || path == \"..\"\n     }\n     func promptRemoval(path string, isDir bool) bool {\n         return false\n     }\n     func shouldPromptOnce(paths []string, opts options) bool {\n         return false\n     }\n     ```\n\n   - `cmd/rm/rm_test.go` (existing test skeleton to modify)\n     - Has TestDiff with BuildBinary and LookPath(\"grm\") already set up\n     - Empty test slice: `tests := []testutils.DiffTest{}`\n     ```go\n     func TestDiff(t *testing.T) {\n         goBin := testutils.BuildBinary(t, \".\")\n         refBin, err := exec.LookPath(\"grm\")\n         if err != nil {\n             t.Skip(\"reference binary grm not found\")\n         }\n         tests := []testutils.DiffTest{}\n         testutils.RunDiffTests(t, goBin, refBin, tests)\n     }\n     ```\n\n   - `pkg/testutils/difftest.go` (reference - provided in project_context)\n     - DiffTest struct: Name, Args, Stdin, Env, WorkDir, ExitCode, Normalize, ExpectedFiles\n     - RunDiffTests runs each test as subtest comparing Go vs reference binary\n     - buildEnv sets LC_ALL=C by default\n     - WorkDir defaults to t.TempDir() if empty\n\n4. Errors and fixes:\n   - No errors yet - I had just finished reading the three required files and was about to plan and implement.\n\n5. Problem Solving:\n   - Read the SRD to understand R1.1-R1.4 requirements\n   - Read existing contract stubs to understand what's already in place (flag parsing is done, stubs need filling)\n   - Read test skeleton to understand the differential testing pattern\n   - Was about to plan implementation approach when interrupted for summarization\n\n6. All user messages:\n   - Message 1: The massive task description including role, repository_files, project_context (vision, architecture, specifications, roadmap, analysis, source_code, requirement_states), execution_constitution, go_style_constitution, task description with required_reading/files/requirements/design_decisions/acceptance_criteria, shared_protocols, package_contracts. The core instruction is to implement R1.1-R1.4 of srd058-rm.\n   - Message 2: \"CRITICAL: Respond with TEXT ONLY. Do NOT call any tools.\" - Request for a conversation summary.\n\n7. Pending Tasks:\n   - Implement `removeFiles()` function in cmd/rm/main.go: iterate paths, check dot/dotdot (R1.3), stat files, refuse directories without -r (R1.2), remove files (R1.1), handle errors and continue (R1.4), track exit code\n   - Implement `removeFile()` function: call os.Remove on a single file\n   - Keep `removeDir()`, `removeEmptyDir()`, `promptRemoval()`, `shouldPromptOnce()` as stubs that compile but are not fully functional (R2-R3 scope)\n   - Add differential test ca